          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Early discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite+quantum+systems"} composite quantum systems
            and their
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+entanglement"} quantum entanglement
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erwin+Schr%C3%B6dinger"}> Erwin Schrödinger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Discussion of Probability Relations between Separated Systems
              %strong 31
              4 (1935) 555-563 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100013554"}> doi:10.1017/S0305004100013554
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Introduction and review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teiko+Heinosaari"}> Teiko Heinosaari
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%A1rio+Ziman"} Mário Ziman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Mathematical Language of Quantum Theory – From Uncertainty to Entanglement
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139031103"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139031103
            %li
              %p
                Dagmar Bruss,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Characterizing entanglement
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0110078"} arXiv:quant-ph/0110078
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.1494474"} doi
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"}> Ingemar Bengtsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+%C5%BByczkowski"} Karol Życzkowski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometry of Quantum States — An Introduction to Quantum Entanglement
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511535048"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511535048
          %p Extensive survey of the field:
          %ul
            %li
              Ryszard Horodecki, Paweł Horodecki, Michał Horodecki, and Karol Horodecki:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum entanglement
              %strong 81
              (2009) 865 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0702225"}> arXiv:quant-ph/0702225
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.81.865"} doi:10.1103/RevModPhys.81.865
          %p
            As a notion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Watrous"}> John Watrous
              , Chapter 6 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Theory of Quantum Information
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316848142"} doi:10.1017/9781316848142
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~watrous/TQI/"} webpage
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~watrous/TQI/TQI.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            In relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlation"} correlation
          %ul
            %li#LuoLuo03
              Shun-long Luo, You-feng Luo,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Correlation and Entanglement
              %strong 19
              (2003) 581–598
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10255-003-0133-z"} doi:10.1007/s10255-003-0133-z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            and in relation to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+supremacy"} quantum supremacy
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Preskill"}> John Preskill
              \:
              = succeed ":" do
                %em Quantum computing and the entanglement frontier
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Theory of the Quantum World – Proceedings of the 25th Solvay Conference on Physics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.5813"} arXiv:1203.5813
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/8674"} doi:10.1142/8674
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://simons.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/docs/394/preskilljohn.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bei+Zeng"}> Bei Zeng
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xie+Chen"} Xie Chen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duan-Lu+Zhou"} Duan-Lu Zhou
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"} Xiao-Gang Wen
              %p
                Sec. 1 of of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Information+Meets+Quantum+Matter"} Quantum Information Meets Quantum Matter
                    – From Quantum Entanglement to Topological Phases of Many-Body Systems
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.02595"} arXiv:1508.02595
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4939-9084-9"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4939-9084-9
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            Exposition of entanglement as a phenomenon of non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+monoidal+category"} Cartesian
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
          %ul
            %li#Baez04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Quandaries: a Category-Theoretic Perspective
              = succeed "," do
                %em The structural foundations of quantum gravity
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0404040"} arXiv:quant-ph/0404040
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-structural-foundations-of-quantum-gravity-9780199269693"} ISBN:9780199269693
          %p
            A discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics+in+terms+of+dagger-compact+categories"} quantum mechanics in terms of dagger-compact categories
            is in
          %ul
            %li#CoeckeKissinger
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Coecke"}> Bob Coecke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aleks+Kissinger"} Aleks Kissinger
              %em The compositional structure of multipartite quantum entanglement
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.2540"}> arXiv:1002.2540
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              W. Dür, G. Vidal, J. I. Cirac,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Three qubits can be entangled in two inequivalent ways
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 62
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+optics"} quantum optics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Byrnes"}> Tim Byrnes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ebubechukwu+Ilo-Okeke"} Ebubechukwu Ilo-Okeke
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Atom Optics: Theory and Applications to Quantum Technology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.14601"} arXiv:2007.14601
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/quantum-atom-optics/2D867888B5C666D3A936F1C942C99568"} CUP
          %p A connection to algebraic geometry is proposed in
          %ul
            %li
              Frédéric Holweck, Jean-Gabriel Luque, Jean-Yves Thibon,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric descriptions of entangled states by auxiliary varieties
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 53
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.4753989"} doi
          %p
            The following work included the consideration of identical particles into the study of quantum entanglement. In this case, the usage of partial trace may not be suitable and instead subsystems are described in terms of subalgebras. The work is in operator algebraic framework, based on usage of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GNS+construction"} GNS construction
            and related to the consideration of von Neumann entropy.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+P.+Balachandran"}> A. P. Balachandran
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T.+R.+Govindarajan"} T. R. Govindarajan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Entanglement and particle identity: a unifying approach
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.0688"} arxiv/1303.0688
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic approach to entanglement and entropy
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.1300"} arxiv/1301.1300
              %em Entanglement, particle identity and the GNS construction: a unifying approach
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/pdf/1205.2882"} arxiv/1205.2882
              (earlier, longer version, overlapping with 1303.0688)
          %p
            Use of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            for quantifying entanglement:
          %ul
            %li#Mainiero2019
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Mainiero"}> Tom Mainiero
              ,
              %em Homological Tools for the Quantum Mechanic
              (2019) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.02011"}> arXiv:1901.02011
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://10.10.11.6/handle/1/1339"} 10.10.11.6/handle/1/1339
          %h3#ReferencesItFromQBit Relating to spacetime
          %p
            Observations and speculations relating quantum entanglement to emergent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            (via something like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality"} AdS/CFT duality
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            = succeed "\u201D):" do
              %a{:href => "holographic+entanglement+entropy#SimonsFoundationItFromQBit"} It from QBit
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Swingle"}> Brian Swingle
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spacetime from Entanglement
                %strong 9
                (2018) 345-358 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-conmatphys-033117-054219"}> doi:10.1146/annurev-conmatphys-033117-054219
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"}> Mark Van Raamsdonk
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spacetime from bits
                %strong 370
                6513 (9 Oct 2020) 198-202 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aay9560"}> doi:10.1126/science.aay9560
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadashi+Takayanagi"}> Tadashi Takayanagi
                \:
                %em Emergent Holographic Spacetime from Quantum Information
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.06595"}> arXiv:2506.06595
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p IAS Workshops on Quantum Information and Spacetime:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "https://www.ias.edu/sns/quantum-information-workshop-2017"} Workshop on Quantum Information and Black Holes, December 5-6, 2017
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "https://www.ias.edu/sns/quantum-information-workshop-2018"} Workshop on Quantum Information and the Structure of Spacetime, December 4-5, 2018
                %li
                  %p
